# CSS Component Token Layer Pattern

**BEFORE editing or creating any CSS file**, apply this pattern:

## Rule: Aggregate All CSS Variables at Top

All component-scoped CSS variables MUST be defined at the **top** of the main component selector:

```css
.component-name {
  /* Component Token Layer - Color Palette */
  --component-title-color: var(--color-text-secondary);
  --component-item-hover-bg: var(--color-ui-active);
  --component-border: var(--color-ui-border);
  
  /* Layout properties below */
  display: flex;
  ...
}
```

## When Creating New CSS Files

1. Start with the Component Token Layer comment
2. Define all color/theme variables first
3. Then add layout/styling properties

## When Editing Existing CSS Files

1. **Check** if tokens are scattered throughout the file
2. **If yes**: Refactor to aggregate them at top of main selector FIRST
3. **Then** make your edits

## DON'T

- ❌ Scatter token definitions throughout the file
- ❌ Use `--theme-*` tokens (use `--color-*` instead)
- ❌ Skip this pattern for "quick fixes"

## Portaled Components (modals, dropdowns, tooltips)

Define tokens in `:root` instead, since portals render outside DOM hierarchy:

```css
:root {
  --component-menu-bg: var(--color-ui-background-elevated);
}
```

